For the homogeneous <linear recurrence relation>, try $u_n=r^n$. Its <characteristic equation of a linear recurrence> is
$$
r^2+3r-4=(r-1)(r+4)=0.
$$
The distinct <roots of a polynomial> $1,-4$ give the complementary terms $A+B(-4)^n$. A constant cannot absorb the forcing because $1$ is already a <root of a polynomial> of the characteristic equation; try a <particular solution> $cn$. Substitution gives $c=-4c+1$, hence $c=1/5$. The <general solution> is $u_n=A+B(-4)^n+n/5$.

The <initial conditions> give $A+B=0$ and $A-4B=4/5$. Hence $A=4/25$, $B=-4/25$, and
$$
\boxed{u_n=\frac n5+\frac4{25}\bigl(1-(-4)^n\bigr),\qquad n\ge0.}
$$

= ii
{parent=a}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=ii}
{c}

The homogeneous <characteristic equation of a linear recurrence> is
$$
r^2+2r+1=(r+1)^2=0.
$$
The <repeated characteristic root of a linear recurrence> $-1$ supplies the independent terms $(-1)^n$ and $n(-1)^n$. A constant <particular solution> is $1/2$, since $1/2=-2(1/2)-1/2+2$. Thus $u_n=1/2+(A+Bn)(-1)^n$.

**The scan prints $u_2=0$, not $u_1=0$. These <initial conditions> are consistent.** They give $A=1/2$ from $u_0=1$, then $0=1/2+A+2B$, so $B=-1/2$. Therefore
$$
\boxed{u_n=\frac12+\frac{1-n}{2}(-1)^n.}
$$
In particular $u_1=1/2$ and $u_2=0$. Direct substitution verifies the <recurrence relation>. This is an example of <nonconsecutive initial values for a linear recurrence>; replacing the printed subscript by 1 would change the answer.

= b
{parent=5}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}
{c}

For <random variables> with finite <second moments>, their <covariance> is
$$
\boxed{\operatorname{Cov}(X,Y)=\mathbb E[(X-\mathbb EX)(Y-\mathbb EY)].}
$$
The <Cauchy-Schwarz inequality> ensures the product is <integrable>. Expand and use <linearity of expectation>:
$$
\begin{aligned}
\operatorname{Cov}(X,Y)
&=\mathbb E[XY]-\mathbb E[X]\mathbb E[Y]
-\mathbb E[X]\mathbb E[Y]+\mathbb E[X]\mathbb E[Y]\\
&=\boxed{\mathbb E[XY]-\mathbb E[X]\mathbb E[Y].}
\end{aligned}
$$
The same identity holds whenever the quantities involved exist with sufficient <integrability>.

= c
{parent=5}
